# Code owners are requested for review automatically, and the `master` ruleset enforces their review.
# Only security- and delivery-critical paths are owned individually; everything else is reviewed under the normal
# pull request rules.
#
# The owner is also the only maintainer. GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull request, so the ruleset
# lets the owner bypass pull request rules when this review is the only unmet rule. GitHub records every bypass.
# See docs/adr/0007-solo-maintainer-governance.md and docs/governance/github-settings.md.
#
# Later entries override earlier ones, and the paths below match the sensitive-path list in the implementation plan.

